.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH GEARS 1 2000-1月 "new" "new"
.SH NAME
new \- create a new GEARS model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fInew(\fBx\fR as <generic> Matrix, 
\fBprior\fR as <generic> PriorNetwork, 
\fBconfig\fR as <generic> GEARSConfig);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
create a new GEARS model
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- 
 the gene expression matrix object of the Perturb-seq experiment data, which 
 could be loaded from a csv table file via the 
 \fBgeneExpression::load.expr\fR api.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior\fB \fR\- 
 the prior knowledge regulatory network object, which could be created by the 
 \fBbnlearn::as.prior_net\fR api: only the gene that is described in this prior 
 network could be mapped into the gene regulatory graph of the GEARS model.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBconfig\fB \fR\- 
 the hyper parameter configuration of the GEARS model, which could be created 
 via the \fBnew("GEARS_opts")\fR syntax in R# environment: the embedding 
 dimension, the hidden layer dimension, the graph convolution layer numbers, 
 the activation function, the learning rate, the epochs, etc.
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a new @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GEARS.GEARS\fR model object that the gene regulatory graph has 
 been created from the given prior network and expression data, the training 
 sample set should be set via the \fBtraining_set\fR api at first and then the 
 model can be trained via the \fBtrain\fR api.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
@\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GEARS.GEARS\fR implements of the interface @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.InsilicoPerturbationExperiment\fR, which could be used as the virtual perturbation experiment container for run knockouts/overexpress/knockdown experiments
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
imports ["GEARS","bnlearn"] from "biosystem";
 imports "geneExpression" from "phenotype_kit";
 
 let exprData = load.expr("./dataset.csv");
 let samples = read.sampleinfo("./experiment.csv");
 let opts = new("GEARS_opts", Activation = "tanh");
 let net = bnlearn::prior_network(
     TF = c(), target_gene = c(), regulation_type = c(), confidence = c(), evidence = c()
 ) |> as.prior_net();
 
 net <- GEARS::new(exprData, net, opts)
 |> training_set(exprData, controls = c(), perturbed = samples)
 |> train()
 ;
 
 make_exports(c( 
    net |> knockouts(c()), 
    net |> overexpress(c()), 
    net |> knockdown(c()) 
 ), dir = "./GNN_result");
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GEARS
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
